 of Galilee and into the region of the Decapolis.","7:32":"Some people brought to Him a man who was deaf and hardly able to speak, and they begged Jesus to place His hand on him.","7:33":"So Jesus took him aside privately, away from the crowd, and put His fingers into the man’s ears. Then He spit and touched the man’s tongue.","7:34":"And looking up to heaven, He sighed deeply and said to him, “Ephphatha!” (which means, “Be opened!”).","7:35":"Immediately the man’s ears were opened and his tongue was released, and he began to speak plainly.","7:36":"Jesus ordered them not to tell anyone. But the more He ordered them, the more widely they proclaimed it.","7:37":"The people were utterly astonished and said, “He has done all things well! He makes even the deaf hear and the mute speak!”"}}},"pairs":{"mt-mk":{"exact":5,"lemma":4,"pctA":14.3,"pctB":8.0,"run":4,"runText":"τὴν θάλασσαν τῆς Γαλιλαίας"}},"minor":[]}